# Keep the build context to the app itself.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE ADDING ANYTHING TO THE DIRECTORY: the Dockerfile does
# `COPY . /app/` in the builder and the runtime image is `COPY --from=builder
# /app/ /app/`. A file sitting here at build time is a file inside the image,
# and `make dev`, `make test` and `docker compose build` all build from this
# directory with whatever an operator has left in it.
#
# .gitignore does NOT help. It governs git and has no bearing on a build
# context, so the two lists have to be kept in step by hand. Everything under
# "secrets and state" below is in .gitignore too, and was reaching the image
# anyway.

.git
.gitignore
*.sw?
.DS_Store

# --- secrets and state -------------------------------------------------------

# .env is the file .env.example tells people to create, and it holds TS_AUTHKEY
# — plus whatever else an operator has put in it. It was landing at /app/.env in
# every locally built image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The workspace: the SQLite database, `share.key` (the HMAC secret behind signed
# upload URLs) and every file anybody has ever shared through this instance.
#
# The bare `*.db` that used to be here did not cover them. Docker matches these
# patterns against the whole path, so `*.db` catches `share.db` at the root and
# sails straight past `data/share.db` — which is where it actually lives.
/data/
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/share.key

# --- bulk that has no business in the context --------------------------------

# Fetched and checksum-verified by the assets stage, then copied in from there.
# A stale local copy would be shadowed by the real one anyway, and mermaid alone
# is 3.5 MB.
/public/assets/mermaid.min.js
/public/assets/github-markdown.css

# Local Perl installs and build scratch, if you build deps outside docker.
local/
.build/

# The browser suite's traces and screenshots. None of it runs in the image.
/e2e/test-results/
/e2e/node_modules/
